# Code owners for the release trust boundary.
#
# This file deliberately does NOT cover the whole repository. Editor, runtime,
# extension, UI, test, and documentation changes are ordinary maintainer
# territory and need only a maintainer's approval.
#
# What is listed here is every path whose contents execute inside a job that
# holds signing or publishing credentials. The signed release build runs
# `pnpm install` (which applies `patches/` and runs the dependency build
# scripts that pnpm-workspace.yaml allows) and then runs
# the electron-builder hooks with Apple notarization and DigiCert credentials in
# the environment. A change to any of those paths can therefore reach those
# credentials on the next tagged release, regardless of who wrote it.
#
# This follows from how the build works, not from a judgment about any
# maintainer. It applies to the project lead's own pull requests on the same
# paths. See MAINTAINERS.md for the public explanation and the exit condition.

# --- Workflow and release definitions ---------------------------------------

/.github/workflows/       @ghinkle
/.github/actions/         @ghinkle
/.github/CODEOWNERS       @ghinkle

# The release job runs generated and helper scripts from this directory, so the
# whole directory is owned rather than an allowlist of filenames that goes stale
# silently as scripts are added.
/scripts/                 @ghinkle

# Release runbooks followed by the release operator. The explicit entries are
# the ones named in the plan; the glob also catches convention-named release
# commands added later, which an allowlist alone would miss.
/.claude/commands/*release*.md          @ghinkle
/.claude/commands/release-alpha.md      @ghinkle
/.claude/commands/promote-public-release.md @ghinkle
/.claude/commands/release-ios.md        @ghinkle
/.claude/commands/ios-release.md        @ghinkle

# --- Code executed by the secret-bearing build, signing, and publish jobs ----

# electron-builder invokes afterPack.js, afterSign.js, and notarize.js with
# APPLE_ID, APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD, MACOS_CERTIFICATE, and the DigiCert
# credentials in the environment.
/packages/electron/build/ @ghinkle

# Applied by pnpm (patchedDependencies) during `pnpm install`.
/patches/                 @ghinkle

# Define what `pnpm install` installs and executes inside the credentialed job.
# pnpm-workspace.yaml carries overrides, patchedDependencies, and allowBuilds
# (which dependencies may run install scripts).
/package.json             @ghinkle
/pnpm-lock.yaml           @ghinkle
/pnpm-workspace.yaml      @ghinkle
/packages/electron/package.json @ghinkle
